# Feature-Based Architecture

All domain-specific business logic, UI components, queries, DTOs, and tRPC routers must be organized inside `src/features/{domain}/`.

### Directory Structure per Feature (`src/features/{domain}/`)

```
src/features/{domain}/
├── components/               # Feature-specific UI components (e.g., project-card.tsx)
├── server/                   # Server-side queries and tRPC routers
│   ├── {domain}-queries.ts   # RSC data fetching and DTO mapping
│   └── {domain}-admin.router.ts # tRPC mutation & query router for admin procedures
├── lib/                      # Feature DTOs, Zod schemas, and data mappers
└── types/                    # Domain-specific TypeScript types
```

### Boundary & Code Sharing Rules

1. **No private cross-feature imports**: `features/projects/` MUST NOT import private internal helpers from `features/certifications/`. Shared code belongs in `src/lib/` or `src/components/shared/`.
2. **Thin App Router pages**: App Router pages in `src/app/` are thin orchestrators. They fetch data via `{domain}-queries.ts` and render feature components.
3. **Router-only helpers**: If helper functions/schemas are only used by one tRPC router, keep them in that router file. Do not split into separate files unless shared across multiple routers.
